    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Runs once per email (from either mailbox, after the merge).\nconst row = $json;\n\nconst SYS = `You are an email triage assistant for a personal inbox. You will be given ONE email's sender, subject, and a short preview/snippet. Score how important it is for the recipient to actually read it, on a 0-10 scale, and classify it into exactly one category.\n\nCategories: health, security, financial, work, personal, scheduling, promotional, newsletter, other.\n\nScoring guidance:\n- 8-10: health/medical results or messages (e.g. lab/diagnostic results, doctor messages, prescription notices), security alerts (login/password/breach), urgent financial deadlines (overdue bills, fraud alerts), time-critical personal/family messages, job interviews.\n- 5-7: work items needing action, appointment confirmations/reminders, non-urgent bills, moderately important personal correspondence.\n- 2-4: informational updates, receipts, low-urgency notifications.\n- 0-1: promotional/marketing emails, sales, newsletters, social-media notifications, spam.\n\nAlways score health results and security alerts high (8+) and promotional/marketing/newsletter content low (0-2), even if the subject line uses urgent-sounding marketing language (\"Last chance!\", \"Sale ends today\", \"24 hours left\").\n\nRespond with ONLY valid JSON, no other text, in exactly this shape:\n{\"score\": <integer 0-10>, \"category\": \"<one category from the list above>\", \"urgent\": <true or false>, \"summary\": \"<one or two plain sentences on what the email is about and why it matters, or why it doesn't>\"}`;\n\nconst USER = `From: ${row.From || 'Unknown'}\\nSubject: ${row.Subject|| '(No Subject)'}\\nPreview: ${row.snippet || '(no preview available)'}`;\n\nconst idx = row.mailboxIndex !== undefined ? row.mailboxIndex : 0;\nconst id = row.id || '';\n\nreturn {\n  id,\n  mailboxIndex: idx,\n  from: row.From || 'Unknown',\n  subject: row.Subject || '(No Subject)',\n  snippet: row.snippet || '',\n  link: id ? `https://mail.google.com/mail/u/${idx}/#all/${id}` : '',\n  messages: [\n    { role: 'system', content: SYS },\n    { role: 'user', content: USER },\n  ],\n};\n"
      },
